{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_6-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_04_420132660", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "Sam Panopoulos claimed to have invented the Hawaiian pizza in 1962.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_58_1261086103#9_1868824840"]}, {"text": "The Toronto Star published a recipe for Spanish pizza in 1962, which included yellow rice and Vienna sausages.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_50_2185395436#5_3005679247"]}, {"text": "Sam Panopoulos was born in Greece and moved to Canada in 1954.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_565495028#8_805625447", "msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_565495028#1_805617132"]}, {"text": "Bacon, ham, and pineapple were not common pizza toppings in the 1960s.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_28_903296016#8_1908570407"]}, {"text": "Sam Panopoulos was inspired by his experience cooking Chinese dishes, including American Chinese food, to create the Hawaiian pizza.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_17_1448273400#1_1598355011"]}, {"text": "The Hawaiian pizza gained widespread popularity after it was invented by Sam Panopoulos in 1962.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_55_75307586#3_191460765"]}, {"text": "There is no evidence that pineapple was used as a pizza topping before 1962.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_50_2185395436#5_3005679247"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_6-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_06_1440134319", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "Instant noodles are a popular global food, but studies suggest they may pose health risks such as stroke and diabetes.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_02_1063111668#3_1804424094"]}, {"text": "TBHQ, a preservative found in instant noodles, could potentially be carcinogenic according to some studies.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_06_1412143852#3_1952026491"]}, {"text": "A study by Hyoun Shin at Harvard School of Public Health found a link between eating instant noodles and an increased risk of metabolic syndrome in women, which can lead to heart conditions and diabetes.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_42_856492098#0_2014485305"]}, {"text": "Instant noodles contain high levels of salt and fat, which can contribute to heart disease according to medical literature.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_42_856492098#0_2014485305"]}, {"text": "Dr. Kuo's study showed that instant noodles remain largely intact in the stomach for hours, unlike homemade noodles which digest much quicker.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_37_589513295#1_1266766038"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_6-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_08_300872161", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The document contains multiple references to superparamagnetic nanoparticles being used in vaccines, which suggests a focus on this topic.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_50_2716323696#10_3857053131"]}, {"text": "There are repeated claims about vaccines causing harm, such as brain damage and neurodegenerative diseases, which suggests a need to verify if these claims are substantiated by credible evidence.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_08_297445435#2_567643066"]}, {"text": "The claim about superparamagnetic nanoparticles being used in vaccines is consistent across various types of media sources, as it is mentioned repeatedly throughout the document.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_50_2716323696#10_3857053131"]}, {"text": "There are numerous references to vaccine-related deaths and adverse reactions in the document, which are serious concerns.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_181663898#4_376585293", "msmarco_v2.1_doc_08_297445435#2_567643066"]}, {"text": "The claims about false flag attacks related to vaccines mentioned in the document do not have any basis in fact as they are not widely accepted or supported by credible sources.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_08_303015497#3_574627886"]}, {"text": "There is no scientific research supporting the use of superparamagnetic nanoparticles in vaccine development and administration as mentioned in the document.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_50_2716323696#10_3857053131"]}, {"text": "There are no official statements or data from health organizations supporting the claims of vaccine-related deaths and adverse reactions mentioned in the document.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_08_303050182#1_574675873"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_6-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_15_116067546", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "Several major technology companies, including Google, Amazon, Microsoft and IBM, are making rapid progress in developing quantum computers.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_20_427175576#2_934187872"]}, {"text": "Google announced a quantum computer with 54 qubits in October 2019, which is the most powerful quantum computer announced in the public domain at that time.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_20_427175576#2_934187872"]}, {"text": "Experts predict that a 4,000 qubit quantum computer could theoretically crack Bitcoin's encryption in a matter of seconds.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_355488050#3_764347568"]}, {"text": "Industry leaders such as Sundar Pichai predict that large-scale quantum computers could be available commercially in five to ten years based on commercially available quantum computers.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_355488050#3_764347568"]}, {"text": "Andersen Cheng suggests that there might be evidence of a more imminent threat within two years based on intelligence world insights.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_355488050#3_764347568"]}, {"text": "Post-quantum cryptography efforts are underway with a competition run by NIST aiming to determine the algorithm for a blockchain resilient to quantum computers.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_355488050#3_764347568"]}]}
