{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_6-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_2529216", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The article discusses the claim that Philipp Budeikin's arrest was largely collapsed due to weak evidence. We need to verify if there are any official statements or reports from law enforcement agencies supporting this claim, as it directly impacts the credibility of the article\u2019s narrative.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_4199697#0_9230250"]}, {"text": "The article states that Budeikin was found sane during his trial, but does not provide details on the court proceedings. We need to verify if there are official records or reports detailing the court's decision.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_22_1129553773#2_2522742759", "msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_4199697#1_9231914", "msmarco_v2.1_doc_37_541331906#0_1166270748"]}, {"text": "The article discusses the claim that Philipp Budeikin was arrested and held in Kresty Prison, Saint Petersburg. We need to verify if this is accurate and find more details about his arrest.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_2413955574#4_2670753539", "msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_2413955574#6_2670758108"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_6-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_7751734", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "Carlos Ghosn's escape from Japan was meticulously planned over several weeks, involving multiple individuals and methods.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_37_618125632#3_1299664145"]}, {"text": "Reports suggest that Ghosn used a combination of train travel to Osaka and a private jet for his journey, possibly through Russian airspace.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_46_105699255#6_248858125"]}, {"text": "Ghosn's legal team maintains that he used a French passport to enter Lebanon, though this has not been confirmed.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_37_618125632#6_1299672578"]}, {"text": "The sequence of events leading up to Ghosn's departure from Japan involved him leaving his house, joining two men at a hotel, and then boarding a train to Osaka before traveling by private jet.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_37_618125632#3_1299664145"]}, {"text": "There are conflicting reports about whether Ghosn wore a hat and surgical mask during his escape, with some sources claiming he did not use such disguises.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_46_105699255#6_248858125"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_6-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_441326441", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "Scientists are critical of the microwave attack theory as an explanation for the Havana syndrome, deeming it implausible.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_738138284#1_829775704"]}, {"text": "The National Academies of Sciences panel found that a directed radio frequency energy attack could be the most plausible explanation for the Havana syndrome, based on the Frey effect mechanism.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_738138284#1_829775704"]}, {"text": "Experts in microwaves and group psychology dismissed the microwave attack theory, calling it 'science fiction'.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_738138284#1_829775704"]}, {"text": "The NAS report emphasized that the findings about a possible microwave attack are far from conclusive and should be taken with caution.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_738138284#1_829775704"]}, {"text": "The report recommended an all-of-government effort to study what happened and anticipate future scenarios, highlighting the need for comprehensive investigation.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_738138284#1_829775704"]}, {"text": "Andrei Pakhomov, a bioengineer from Old Dominion University, expressed skepticism about the microwave theory based on his decades of research in the field.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_738138284#1_829775704"]}, {"text": "The Cuban Academy of Sciences suggested psychogenic effects could be important, but disagreed with the radio frequency pulse finding proposed by the NAS report.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_738138284#1_829775704"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_6-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_1300032609", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "A conservatorship is legally defined as a court case where a judge appoints an individual or organization, called the conservator, to care for someone who 'cannot care' for themselves or who cannot manage their own finances.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_1292466165#1_2369928850"]}, {"text": "Jamie argues that his conservatorship is working. Under his order, his legal team says, Britney's estate has gone from being in debt to having a valuation of more than $60 million.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_880637681#9_1802064106"]}, {"text": "In November 2020, his legal team said Jamie has worked hard to restore Britney to 'good health, reunite her with her children, and revive her career.'", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_880637681#9_1802064106"]}, {"text": "In August 2020, the pop star's court-appointed attorney said Britney 'strongly opposed' her father's position as the sole conservator of her estate and asked the court to limit his control.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_58_884954839#15_1333909187"]}, {"text": "Supporters of Britney Spears outside a Los Angeles courthouse on September 16, 2020. There's even a podcast, Britney's Gram, which is dedicated to dissecting her Instagram and social media posts.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_256517380#12_609653068"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_6-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_38_227081897", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The article mentions a 10-year-old girl from Italy who died after attempting the Blackout Challenge, but no official source is cited.", "citations": []}, {"text": "Medical experts warn that participating in TikTok trends like the Blackout Challenge can lead to fainting, seizures, brain damage, and even death.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_557526820#1_1019680158"]}, {"text": "The article notes that similar trends like the Pass Out Challenge have also been dangerous, suggesting a broader issue with online safety for minors.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_557526820#1_1019680158"]}, {"text": "To report instances of the TikTok blackout challenge, users can click on the arrow next to the video, select 'report,' and choose 'suicide, self-harm, and dangerous acts.'", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_1572491910#11_1769402338"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_6-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_1014551192", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "William 'Rick' Singer was charged with racketeering conspiracy, money laundering conspiracy, conspiracy to defraud the United States, and obstruction of justice.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_47_947823370#1_2051335372"]}, {"text": "The scandal involved 50 people, including wealthy parents, SAT and ACT administrators, college athletics coaches, and a college administrator.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_47_947823370#1_2051335372"]}, {"text": "Parents paid anywhere from $200,000 to $6.5 million to guarantee admission at elite colleges and universities through Singer's services.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_47_947823370#1_2051335372"]}, {"text": "Rick Singer faces a maximum sentence of 65 years in prison, three years of supervised release, and a $1.25 million fine.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_47_947823370#1_2051335372"]}, {"text": "From 2011 to 2019, Singer's 'side door' was open for highly profitable business, in which he collected $25 million dollars.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_47_947823370#1_2051335372"]}, {"text": "The FBI began making arrests in March 2019, starting with actress Felicity Huffman.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_47_947823370#1_2051335372"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_6-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_1165221603", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "Oxygen bars and recreational oxygen inhalers promise to improve your well-being, but the health claims are questionable.", "citations": []}, {"text": "Healthy individuals do not need extra oxygen as their blood can only hold a certain amount, according to Dr. Jason Turowski.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_750898507#9_949877356"]}, {"text": "The numerous health claims made by oxygen bars, such as reducing stress or improving cognitive function, lack scientific support according to experts like Dr. Norman H. Edelman.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_750898507#9_949877356"]}, {"text": "Oxygen bars may pose health risks, especially for individuals with existing lung conditions or using medical-grade oxygen.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_07_1018983456#4_1810842562"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_6-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_41_1960853470", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "Cancer researchers in Israel have found that certain varieties of cannabis can kill brain and breast cancer cells without harming healthy cells nearby, according to Dr. David Meiri's research.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_45_603374908#3_1083853233"]}, {"text": "Dr. Abrams from UCSF Osher Center for Integrative Medicine cautions that despite anecdotal success stories, there is insufficient evidence from large-scale clinical trials to recommend cannabis as a cure for cancer.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_00_878865573#0_1631318126"]}, {"text": "A comprehensive review by the National Academies of Sciences, Engineering and Medicine found insufficient evidence to say that cannabis can treat cancer directly without large-scale, placebo-controlled clinical trials.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_38_1204380494#2_2433315245"]}, {"text": "While preclinical data suggests potential efficacy, experts caution against forgoing traditional treatments as more research is needed to fully understand how cannabinoids can be used in treating various types of cancer.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_37_471128432#2_1003882594"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_6-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_42_654618974", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The Mandela Effect occurs when a large group of people believe an event occurred when it did not, as exemplified by Fiona Broome's belief that Nelson Mandela died in the 1980s (1).", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_181279329#1_375761348"]}, {"text": "Broome found that other people shared her belief, leading to the term 'Mandela effect' being coined (2).", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_2745451335#0_3107716807"]}, {"text": "Doctors explain the Mandela Effect as a form of confabulation, where people create false memories without intending to deceive (3).", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_23_265890181#0_606911467"]}, {"text": "Examples include remembering 'Berenstein Bears' as 'The Berenstain Bears,' and 'Jif' as 'Jiffy' (4).", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_05_909876184#3_1515333317"]}, {"text": "While the term was coined by Fiona Broome, it gained attention through social media and online communities (5).", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_33_1317756161#9_2805299747"]}]}
