{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_6-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_1289995263", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The New York Times reported on a Twitter hack involving the theft of accounts from celebrities and other users.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_58_748319457#2_1059491112"]}, {"text": "The hack targeted 130 accounts, including those of celebrities like Barack Obama and Elon Musk.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_58_748319457#2_1059491112"]}, {"text": "A 17-year-old Florida teenager named Graham Ivan Clark was charged as the mastermind behind the Twitter hack.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_58_748319457#2_1059491112"]}, {"text": "The hack embarrassed Twitter and raised questions about the security provided by tech companies.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_58_748319457#2_1059491112"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_6-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_52_1666095905", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The proposed Super League would significantly impact smaller clubs and leagues in Europe by potentially disrupting the traditional promotion and relegation system, which is a core part of European football's pyramid structure.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_10_83725357#2_161679418"]}, {"text": "Florentino Perez claims that the Super League will provide greater economic growth and support for the wider football pyramid via long-term commitment to uncapped solidarity payments, which will grow in line with league revenues.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_10_83725357#2_161679418"]}, {"text": "UEFA has threatened legal action against the Super League, warning that players involved in it will be banned from playing in the World Cup and Euros.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_10_83725357#2_161679418"]}, {"text": "Florentino Perez stated that the Super League will help football at every level and take it to its rightful place in the world by bringing together the world's greatest clubs and players to play each other throughout the season, ensuring world-class competition and facilities.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_10_83725357#2_161679418"]}, {"text": "Critics argue that the proposed Super League threatens the tradition and history of European football by prioritizing financial gains over fair competition, potentially alienating fans and damaging smaller clubs.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_10_83725357#2_161679418"]}, {"text": "According to Florentino Perez, the proposed Super League aims to help overcome financial difficulties faced by football clubs through significantly greater economic growth and support for European football via long-term commitment to uncapped solidarity payments that will grow in line with league revenues.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_10_83725357#2_161679418"]}, {"text": "Alex Ferguson criticized the proposed Super League as a piece of nonsense that has done no good for club reputations and alienated many supporters, emphasizing the importance of fan support in football.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_10_83725357#2_161679418"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_6-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_54_304836636", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "Electronic payments aren't as private as cash payments.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_45_1177368547#1_2366573538"]}, {"text": "Cash allows you to spend money and receive funds anonymously.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_45_1177368547#1_2366573538"]}, {"text": "Sweden is gearing up to become the first cashless nation in the world, with an economy 100 percent digital by 2023.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_837066867#1_1724944735"]}, {"text": "Cash transactions accounted for just 1% of Sweden's GDP in 2019, and cash withdrawals have been steadily declining by about 10% per year.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_837066867#1_1724944735"]}, {"text": "India banned 500 and 1,000 rupee notes in November 2016, in an effort to catch criminals and those working in the informal economy.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_40_971119848#10_1993192918"]}, {"text": "While these two examples had varying levels of success, both countries struggled to address how the marginalized would fare in a 100% cashless society.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_22_1067298671#9_2378663297"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_6-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_54_1547893878", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The 'Birds Aren't Real' conspiracy theory originated from a specific group of individuals who spread it through social media and campus events at the University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_33_747519998#2_1547117957"]}, {"text": "The target audience for this conspiracy theory includes college students and young adults who are active on social media platforms.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_33_747519998#2_1547117957"]}, {"text": "The 'Birds Aren't Real' conspiracy theory has been spread through social media posts, campus events, and word-of-mouth among students at the University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_33_747519998#2_1547117957"]}, {"text": "The 'Birds Aren't Real' conspiracy theory claims that birds are actually drones or surveillance devices used by the government for monitoring purposes.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_33_747519998#2_1547117957"]}, {"text": "The 'Birds Aren't Real' conspiracy theory is not directly connected to other specific conspiracy theories but shares some themes with broader surveillance and government control narratives.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_33_747519998#2_1547117957"]}, {"text": "The 'Birds Aren't Real' conspiracy theory has gained significant attention on social media platforms among college students and young adults in the United States.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_33_747519998#2_1547117957"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_6-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_55_248024230", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "Apple has become what it once railed against: the behemoth seeking to control markets, block competition, and stifle innovation.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_531689358#2_1053021223"]}, {"text": "Apple impose[s] unreasonable and unlawful restraints to completely monopolize both markets and prevent software developers from reaching the over one billion users of its mobile devices (e.g., iPhone and iPad) unless they go through a single store controlled by Apple, the App Store.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_531689358#2_1053021223"]}, {"text": "Apple is bigger, more powerful, more entrenched, and more pernicious than the monopolists of yesteryear.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_531689358#2_1053021223"]}, {"text": "Apple requires software developers who wish to sell in-app content to go through a single store controlled by Apple, the App Store, where Apple exacts an oppressive 30% tax on the sale of every app.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_531689358#2_1053021223"]}, {"text": "Apple has become what it once railed against: the behemoth seeking to control markets, block competition, and stifle innovation. Apple is bigger, more powerful, more entrenched, and more pernicious than the monopolists of yesteryear.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_531689358#2_1053021223"]}, {"text": "Apple impose[s] unreasonable and unlawful restraints to completely monopolize both markets and prevent software developers from reaching the over one billion users of its mobile devices (e.g., iPhone and iPad) unless they go through a single store controlled by Apple, the App Store.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_531689358#2_1053021223"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_6-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_57_933363597", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "Jackfruit is a good source of fiber, which could help you feel fuller for longer and keep your bowel movements regular.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_46_808496648#7_1718139116"]}, {"text": "One study found that jackfruit extract made it easier for people with diabetes to control their blood sugar levels, supporting WebMD's claim about managing blood sugar.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_46_808496648#7_1718139116"]}, {"text": "Jackfruit is rich in vitamin C and contains B vitamins, which are important for overall health.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_46_808496648#7_1718139116"]}, {"text": "The natural chemicals in jackfruit may help prevent stomach ulcers and have anti-inflammatory effects, according to the article.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_46_808496648#7_1718139116"]}, {"text": "Jackfruit contains many antioxidants that can help delay or prevent cell damage in your body, as mentioned in the article.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_46_808496648#7_1718139116"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_6-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_58_748655897", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The 2019 'Storm Area 51' event aimed to challenge government secrecy.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_1633088417#3_3429253226"]}, {"text": "Area 51's official name is Nevada Test and Training Range at Groom Lake but remains culturally significant.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_1633088417#3_3429253226"]}, {"text": "Conspiracy theories about Area 51 have persisted since the 1950s, reflecting broader cultural changes.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_1633088417#3_3429253226"]}, {"text": "The 2019 event drew attention to Area 51, challenging government secrecy efforts.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_1633088417#3_3429253226"]}, {"text": "Secrecy around Area 51 is maintained due to classified military operations, impacting public understanding.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_1633088417#3_3429253226"]}, {"text": "Conspiracy theories influence media coverage and public interest in Area 51's activities.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_1633088417#3_3429253226"]}, {"text": "Organizers aimed to demonstrate Area 51 was not inviolable through the 2019 event.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_1633088417#3_3429253226"]}, {"text": "The name 'Area 51' was officially used in the 1950s but gained cultural significance later.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_1633088417#3_3429253226"]}, {"text": "Conspiracy theories have kept public interest high, leading to ongoing media coverage and events.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_1633088417#3_3429253226"]}, {"text": "Maintaining secrecy has benefits for military operations but limits public understanding.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_1633088417#3_3429253226"]}]}
